# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
#
# Order matters. Specific 301 redirects (renamed pages) come FIRST.
# Catch-all slug rewrites come LAST so they only fire when no real
# file or dedicated static page matches the request.

# ─── Renamed pages (permanent 301) ───
# Series page renamed 2026-05-13: "West Side Card Show" → "West Side Show"
/shows/west-side-card-show       /shows/west-side-show         301
/shows/west-side-card-show.html  /shows/west-side-show         301

# ─── Catch-all slug rewrites (status 200 = silent rewrite, URL stays clean) ───
# /shows/<slug> → show.html?slug=<slug>. Only fires for paths that aren't
# already a real file (Cloudflare Pages serves static files first).
# Lets us have clean URLs like /shows/pokemon-rave for one-off events
# that don't have a dedicated static page.
/shows/:slug                     /shows/show.html?slug=:slug   200
